1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
South Korea is in East Asia.

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:05,140
It is on the southern part of the Korean Peninsula.

3
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:09,140
A peninsula is land with water on three sides.

4
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:11,600
Seoul is the capital city.

5
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:14,200
The Han River goes through the city area.

6
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:20,460
Many people know Seoul for music, cafes, fashion, shopping, and fast trains.

7
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:24,980
This lesson uses named places instead of one simple image.

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:36,220
Gyeongbokgung Palace teaches royal history, Gwangjang Market shows market food, Myeong-dong shows visitor shopping, and the Han River gives open city space.

9
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:38,800
Use real names to make the map clear.

10
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:45,040
Gyeongbokgung Palace and Gwanghwamun Square show royal history near the old center of Seoul.

11
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:50,480
Bukchon Hanok Village and Insa-dong are nearby culture areas.

12
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:53,160
Gwangjang Market is a food-market name.

13
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:58,780
Myeong-dong, Namdaemun Market, and Dongdaemun are shopping names, but each one has a different job.

14
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,380
The Han River is also important because it is a real line through the city.

15
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:10,980
A visitor can plan a day around palace history, market food, shopping streets, and river or tower views.

16
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,720
Seoul becomes easier to understand when each name has a purpose.

17
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:19,740
Gyeongbokgung Palace is not just "an old place."

18
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,840
It was the first main palace of the Joseon dynasty in Seoul.

19
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:30,180
It teaches royal history, government history, gates, courtyards, and palace buildings.

20
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:39,620
Near it, Gwanghwamun Square has a large public space and the statue of King Sejong, an important Korean king.

21
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:43,040
Bukchon Hanok Village is also specific.

22
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:46,880
It sits between Gyeongbokgung Palace and Changdeokgung Palace.

23
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:55,780
A hanok is a traditional Korean house, and Bukchon shows hanok roofs and narrow streets close to modern Seoul.

24
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:02,900
Insa-dong is nearby and is useful for crafts, tea, small shops, and traditional culture.

25
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:06,300
N Seoul Tower is a different kind of place.

26
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:11,940
It is on Namsan Mountain, so it teaches the idea of a city-view point.

27
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:16,760
From there, Seoul looks like roads, buildings, hills, and lights.

28
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:24,960
The Han River parks show another real side of the city: people walk, ride bikes, rest, and meet friends near the water.

29
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:28,000
These names teach a simple idea.

30
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:30,720
Gyeongbokgung is for royal history.

31
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,420
Bukchon is for hanok streets.

32
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:37,140
Insa-dong is for traditional shops and tea.

33
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:40,640
N Seoul Tower is for a high city view.

34
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:43,660
The Han River is for open public space.

35
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,100
Food in Seoul is not only one thing.

36
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:48,920
The place changes the meal.

37
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:59,800
A visitor can eat in Gwangjang Market, a small restaurant, a cafe, a department-store food hall, or a street-food area in Myeong-dong.

38
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,400
Gwangjang Market is the main example for market food.

39
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:05,860
It is known for a busy food street with many choices.

40
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:13,880
A visitor may see bindaetteok, a mung bean pancake, plus gimbap, handmade noodles, bibimbap, and other dishes.

41
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:20,380
Some stalls also sell yukhoe, a raw beef dish, so visitors should choose what feels comfortable.

42
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:26,900
For a sit-down meal, common examples include bulgogi, bibimbap, and samgyeopsal.

43
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:30,840
Bulgogi is thinly sliced marinated beef.

44
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:34,500
Bibimbap is rice with vegetables and other toppings.

45
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,080
Samgyeopsal is grilled pork belly.

46
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:41,200
These examples show that Korean food is not one taste.

47
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:42,940
Some food is spicy.

48
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,700
Some food is mild.

49
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,440
Some meals are quick.

50
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:48,940
Some meals are slow and social.

51
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:53,640
Shopping in Seoul is easier when you know the job of each district.

52
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:57,800
Myeong-dong is one of Seoul's main visitor shopping areas.

53
00:03:58,260 --> 00:04:04,400
Many visitors go there for clothes, cosmetics, shoes, accessories, department stores, and street food.

54
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:07,000
Namdaemun Market is different.

55
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:11,780
The Seoul tourism guide describes it as Korea's largest traditional market.

56
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:18,480
It is near the old Namdaemun gate area and is useful for many kinds of goods, food, and small shops.

57
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:23,920
Dongdaemun is another shopping name, but its job is fashion.

58
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:34,140
The Seoul tourism guide describes Dongdaemun Market as a very large wholesale and retail shopping district, with many malls, specialty shops, and clothing-related businesses.

59
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:42,940
Hongdae is different again: it is known for youth culture, music, cafes, fashion, and a lively street feeling.

60
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:47,700
A visitor can get confused when every district is called a shopping area.

61
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:51,020
The name is similar, but the job is different.

62
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:54,920
Myeong-dong is useful for visitor-friendly shopping and cosmetics.

63
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:57,500
Namdaemun is a traditional market.

64
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:01,780
Dongdaemun is connected with fashion supply and big shopping buildings.

65
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:05,700
Hongdae is for a cafe, music, and youth-culture walk.

66
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,960
A simple travel day in Seoul can use real names.

67
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:13,540
In the morning, visit Gyeongbokgung Palace, then walk toward Gwanghwamun Square.

68
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:18,280
If you want quieter streets, choose Bukchon Hanok Village.

69
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:23,480
If you want crafts, tea, and small shops, choose Insa-dong.

70
00:05:23,480 --> 00:05:31,540
At lunch, choose Gwangjang Market for a busy market-food experience, or choose a small restaurant for bulgogi, bibimbap, or samgyeopsal.

71
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:40,940
In the afternoon, choose Myeong-dong for cosmetics and visitor shopping, Namdaemun Market for a traditional market, or Dongdaemun for fashion shopping.

72
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:50,860
In the evening, choose N Seoul Tower for a high city view or a Han River park for an open walk near the water.

73
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,240
This plan is simple, but it helps.

74
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:59,160
Seoul is large, so ten places in one day can become too much.

75
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:09,220
One palace or hanok area, one food place, one shopping district, and one view or river stop give the day a clear shape.
